{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And you shall purge the innocent blood.</b> As its Targum renders: 'shedder of innocent blood,' or 'its punishment,' as in the phrase 'do not grant innocent blood' — that is, the punishment of innocent blood. <b>When you do what is right in the eyes of YHWH,</b> that is, in the eyes of YHWH who redeemed you from Egypt on this condition — on condition that you do what is right in the eyes of YHWH. And likewise He mentioned 'whom YHWH redeemed,' for the bringing out and redemption from Egypt was through the great Name, and for this reason it did not say 'in the eyes of YHWH your Elohim' as is the usage throughout the parashah and likewise in most of Deuteronomy. And the sense of the verse is that one who eliminates murderers from the world does what is right in the eyes of YHWH." "<b>And it is possible</b> to interpret further that this verse is a promise for the future: it says, if you do what is right in the eyes of YHWH, you shall purge the shedder of blood, for no shedder of innocent blood will be found in the land — for by virtue of this the time to come will draw near, when all murder and all war shall cease from the world, as the prophet, peace be upon him, promised that wars shall cease, as it says (Isaiah 2:4): ״וכתתו חרבותיהם לאתים וחניתותיהם למזמרות לא ישא גוי אל גוי חרב ולא ילמדו עוד מלחמה״. Then rest and peace shall abound in the world for Israel, who are a people set apart and are called Shulamite, as it says (Song of Songs 7:1): ״שובי שובי השולמית״. And they shall sacrifice to the unique Name, exalted be He, who is called Peace, as it says (Judges 6:24): ״ויקרא לו ה׳ שלום״. And they shall offer burnt offerings and peace offerings in the city called Peace, as it says (Genesis 33:18): ״ויבא יעקב שלם״. And they shall merit the perfection of body and soul through the observance of the Torah, whose entirety is peace, as Solomon, peace be upon him, said (Proverbs 3:17): ״דרכיה דרכי נועם וכל נתיבותיה שלום״."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:49:52.380311282Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}